FB = FA [05]
DA ∥ EG [06]
DG ∥ AE [07]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. C,A,E are collinear [02] & EG ∥ AD [06] & DG ∥ AE [07] ⇒  ∠GEA = ∠ADG [08]
002. C,A,E are collinear [02] & DG ∥ AE [07] ⇒  ∠GAE = ∠AGD [09]
003. ∠GEA = ∠ADG [08] & ∠GAE = ∠AGD [09] (Similar Triangles)⇒  AE = GD [10]
004. AE = GD [10] & EC = EA [03] ⇒  CE = DG [11]
005. C,B,D are collinear [00] & DB = DC [01] ⇒  D is midpoint of CB [12]
006. C,A,E are collinear [02] & EC = EA [03] ⇒  E is midpoint of CA [13]
007. D is midpoint of CB [12] & E is midpoint of CA [13] ⇒  DE ∥ BA [14]
008. B,A,F are collinear [04] & DE ∥ AB [14] ⇒  ∠FDE = ∠DFB [15]
009. B,A,F are collinear [04] & FB = FA [05] ⇒  F is midpoint of BA [16]
010. E is midpoint of CA [13] & F is midpoint of BA [16] ⇒  EF ∥ CB [17]
011. C,B,D are collinear [00] & B,A,F are collinear [04] & EF ∥ BC [17] & DE ∥ AB [14] ⇒  ∠FED = ∠DBF [18]
012. ∠FDE = ∠DFB [15] & ∠FED = ∠DBF [18] (Similar Triangles)⇒  FE = DB [19]
013. D is midpoint of CB [12] & F is midpoint of BA [16] ⇒  DF ∥ CA [20]
014. DF ∥ AC [20] & DG ∥ AE [07] & C,A,E are collinear [02] ⇒  DG ∥ DF [21]
015. DG ∥ DF [21] ⇒  G,D,F are collinear [22]
016. C,A,E are collinear [02] & G,D,F are collinear [22] & C,B,D are collinear [00] & AC ∥ DF [20] & EF ∥ BC [17] ⇒  ∠CEF = ∠GDB [23]
017. CE = DG [11] & FE = DB [19] & ∠CEF = ∠GDB [23] (SAS)⇒  FC = BG
